From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Apr 2026 18:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: xilinx: dma: initialize mplane height and plane count

The Xilinx DMA capture driver initializes the default multiplanar format
without setting the frame height or the number of planes. Userspace then
sees invalid defaults such as 1920x0 with zero planes, and VIDIOC_REQBUFS
fails with -EINVAL before streaming can start.

Initialize the default multiplanar height and plane count from the driver
defaults and the selected format description.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-dma.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-dma.c b/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-dma.c
index 7851b0d0d8a5..ab9b58538189 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-dma.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-dma.c
@@ -1272,6 +1272,8 @@ int xvip_dma_init(struct xvip_composite_device *xdev, struct xvip_dma *dma,
 		pix_mp->pixelformat = dma->fmtinfo->fourcc;
 		pix_mp->colorspace = V4L2_COLORSPACE_SRGB;
 		pix_mp->field = V4L2_FIELD_NONE;
 		pix_mp->width = XVIP_DMA_DEF_WIDTH;
+		pix_mp->height = XVIP_DMA_DEF_HEIGHT;
+		pix_mp->num_planes = dma->fmtinfo->buffers;
 
 		/* Handling contiguous data with mplanes */
 		if (dma->fmtinfo->buffers == 1) {
-- 
